# Ignore rules for apps/backend/Dockerfile.
#
# Named `Dockerfile.dockerignore` on purpose: the build context is the helix-x
# workspace root (so ../../framework resolves), and BuildKit reads this file
# instead of a `.dockerignore` at that root. Paths are relative to the
# workspace root.
#
# Allow-list: exclude everything, then re-include only what the backend image
# needs. Anything new has to be added here deliberately — which is how local
# .env secrets and the SQLite database stay out of the image.

*

# Framework packages, as packed tarballs (`pnpm run pack` in helix-x-backend).
!framework/helix-x-backend/.artifacts/*.tgz

# Workspace manifests: the lockfile resolves every importer.
!example/helix-x-rawla/package.json
!example/helix-x-rawla/pnpm-lock.yaml
!example/helix-x-rawla/pnpm-workspace.yaml
!example/helix-x-rawla/tsconfig.base.json
!example/helix-x-rawla/apps/frontend/package.json
!example/helix-x-rawla/packages/client-sdk/package.json

# The backend itself.
!example/helix-x-rawla/apps/backend

# …minus local state, build output and anything that is not source.
example/helix-x-rawla/apps/backend/node_modules
example/helix-x-rawla/apps/backend/dist
example/helix-x-rawla/apps/backend/data
example/helix-x-rawla/apps/backend/coverage
example/helix-x-rawla/apps/backend/.turbo
example/helix-x-rawla/apps/backend/.env
example/helix-x-rawla/apps/backend/.env.*
example/helix-x-rawla/apps/backend/**/*.tsbuildinfo
example/helix-x-rawla/apps/backend/**/*.spec.ts
**/.DS_Store
